            <ArticleTitle>[Treatment in perforation of the dura by catheter during peridural anesthesia in obstetrics (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>284-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A rare complication following a dural tap in labour is reported: cerebrospinal fluid was aspirated although a catheter was properly re-inserted into the peridural space. The most successful therapy is proposed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
